# Documentation maintenance

Applies when editing schema, routes, API clients, or app routing. Prefer skill [docs-sync-during-work](mdc:.cursor/skills/docs-sync-during-work/SKILL.md) for the full gate.

- New or changed REST route: add/update **one row** in [docs/reference/api.md](mdc:docs/reference/api.md).
- Model or relation change: update [docs/reference/domain.md](mdc:docs/reference/domain.md).
- New route/page or API client module: update [docs/reference/frontend.md](mdc:docs/reference/frontend.md).
- Auth/FX/architecture change: update [docs/explanation/architecture.md](mdc:docs/explanation/architecture.md) only if behavior changed.
- Primary code path moves: update [docs/meta/code-map.md](mdc:docs/meta/code-map.md).
- Hub / agent index: [docs/README.md](mdc:docs/README.md), [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).
- Never link to `plans/` from committed documentation (`README.md`, `docs/*`, `AGENTS.md`). That directory is gitignored local WIP.

Skip doc updates for trivial changes (typo, CSS-only, comment-only).

Do **not** expand `golden-rule.mdc` or `project-context.mdc` per feature — only when global conventions change.

Keep entries short (table rows); no full JSON examples in docs. New pages need Diátaxis YAML front matter (`diataxis`, `use_when`, `audience`) — see skill `docs-author`.

Old flat paths (`docs/api.md`, etc.) are redirect stubs; edit the canonical file under `docs/reference|how-to|explanation|tutorials|meta/`.
